{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel were in the desert.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said: had Israel observed the second Sabbath, no nation or tongue would have ruled over them. And how do they know that this was on the second Sabbath? From the fact that it is written ויהיו וימצאו — immediately after they were commanded the commandment of the Sabbath, they found a gatherer. And how do we know that this gatherer was Zelophehad? From the fact that it is written מקושש עצים ביום השבת — עצי״ם with two yods in דביו״ם rises in gematria to צלפחד. And why was the section of the gatherer juxtaposed to the section of tzitzit? Because at the time the gatherer desecrated the Sabbath, Moses said before the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the Universe, it is written regarding tefillin למען תהיה תורת ה׳ בפיך, and You commanded not to carry them on the Sabbath — he was carrying them, he would have been reminded and would not have desecrated the Sabbath. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: I hereby ordain and command them one commandment through which they will be reminded of the commandments, just as with the commandment of tefillin, and which will be practiced on the Sabbath — and this is the commandment of tzitzit."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:32.751899252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}